# KQL Query Structure

A KQL query typically follows a pipeline model.

```kusto
TableName
| Operator
| Operator
| Operator
```

Each operator processes the output of the previous step.

Example:

```kusto
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize FailedLogins = count() by Account
| order by FailedLogins desc
```

---

# Understanding Tables

All data in Log Analytics Workspace is stored in tables.

Examples include:

| Table | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| SecurityEvent | Windows security logs |
| Syslog | Linux system logs |
| AzureActivity | Azure administrative events |
| SigninLogs | Microsoft Entra ID sign-ins |
| Heartbeat | Agent health |
| CommonSecurityLog | Firewall events |
| MeridianLogs_CL | Custom authentication logs (Project) |

Each row represents an event, while columns describe the event's attributes.

---

# Essential KQL Operators

## where

Filters records that meet specific conditions.

Example:

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData contains "Failed password"
```

---

## project

Selects specific columns.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, RawData
```

---

## extend

Creates calculated columns.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)", 1, RawData)
```

---

## summarize

Aggregates data.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| summarize Attempts = count() by Computer
```

---

## sort / order by

Sorts results.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| summarize Attempts = count() by Computer
| order by Attempts desc
```

---

## top

Returns the highest-ranking records.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| summarize Attempts = count() by Computer
| top 5 by Attempts
```

---

## distinct

Returns unique values.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| distinct Computer
```

---

## take

Returns a sample of records.

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| take 10
```

---

# Working with Time

Time is critical during investigations.

Example:

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
```

Other examples:

```kusto
ago(1h)
ago(7d)
ago(30d)
```

---

# String Searching

Common operators include:

```kusto
contains
has
startswith
endswith
matches regex
```

Example:

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed"
```

---

# Parsing Log Data

Many security logs contain valuable information within text fields.

Example log:

```
Failed password for invalid user admin from 203.0.113.77 port 22 ssh2
```

Extract the source IP:

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)",1,RawData)
```

Extract usernames:

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| extend Username = extract(@"user ([a-zA-Z0-9_-]+)",1,RawData)
```

Parsing transforms raw text into structured fields that can be used in detections and investigations.

