# Performance Best Practices

Efficient queries improve investigation speed and reduce resource usage.

Recommendations:

- Filter data early using `where`.
- Limit time ranges with `ago()`.
- Select only required columns using `project`.
- Avoid unnecessary wildcard searches.
- Use `summarize` instead of manual counting.
- Test queries on smaller datasets before running them across large environments.

---

# Common Mistakes

Avoid these common issues:

- Searching all historical data without a time filter.
- Returning unnecessary columns.
- Using broad text searches that increase execution time.
- Ignoring null or empty values.
- Building detections without validating query results.

